## 3. ✨ Add support for setting default values for `response_model` formatting
URL: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/6041

This PR is a follow up on this PR: https://github.com/tiangolo/fastapi/pull/2187 that was never merged 

This would allow for setting the default value of `response_model_by_alias`, `response_model_exclude_unset`, `response_model_exclude_defaults` and `response_model_exclude_none` at an application or at a router level, rather than on each individual endpoint. 

This is useful in cases where a consistent non-default behavior is desired across all endpoints and saves the need to declare so in each endpoint. 


## Timeline
...
> **Orb Code Review** (powered by GLM 5.1 on [Orb Cloud](https://orbcloud.dev))
> 
> ## Summary
> 
> This PR adds the ability to set default values for `response_model_by_alias`, `response_model_exclude_unset`, `response_model_exclude_defaults`, and `response_model_exclude_none` at both the `FastAPI` app level and `APIRouter` level. Route-level settings take precedence over router-level, which takes precedence over app-level.
> 
> ## Architecture
> 
> The implementation uses the existing `Default()` / `DefaultPlaceholder` pattern to distinguish between "not explicitly set" and "explicitly set to True/False". The cascade resolution is: route parameter → router default → app default. This is clean and consistent with how `response_class` and `generate_unique_id_function` already work.
> 
> Key additions:
> - 4 new parameters on both `FastAPI.__init__()` and `APIRouter.__init__()`
> - `get_value_or_default_value()` helper in `fastapi/utils.py`
> - `include_router()` correctly resolves the cascade from included routes
> 
> ## Issues
> 
> ### 1. Type annotation mismatch in decorator methods (Warning)
> 
> **Files:** `fastapi/applications.py`, `fastapi/routing.py`
> 
> The route decorator methods (`.get()`, `.post()`, etc.) declare the parameter type as `bool` but use `Default(True)` as the default value:
> ```python
> response_model_by_alias: bool = Default(True) # type says bool, value is DefaultPlaceholder
> ```
> 
> Meanwhile, `add_api_route()`...

